## Caveats (what NOT to flag)

- Technical-literal uses of a banned word (key as API key, load-bearing in structural engineering, delve in archaeology, navigating as actual navigation).
- "holistic" is banned as marketing filler ("a holistic approach") but allowed for a genuine whole-system property. This is the general meaning-versus-decoration condition that governs the erudite register in voice-authoring.md.
- Direct quotes from sources using a banned phrase.
- Single instances of antithesis, triplet, or hedge constructions. Density is the tell.
- Informal registers (chat, casual email) where a relaxed voice is appropriate.
- Documents that teach this list, including this file, the profile, and any text that names the patterns. Flag only the prose proper.
- The "quiet / quietly" material inside prior published titles ("When Governance Works Quietly") or inside quotes of prior work.
- "quite" is an accepted softener / downtoner in his register ("quite welcome"), not a banned booster like "very" or "really." Confirmed on the 2026-07-20 Bernard reply.

